cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it as below."
title: "Augur: Measuring When Predicting Data Makes It Faster to Move"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CygnusXl/Augur"
authors:
  - family-names: Hansen
    given-names: Peter
    email: peterhansen6002@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A testbed that measures whether predicting data makes it faster to store and
  transfer: a prefetch scheduler with sequential, stride and Markov predictors,
  a trace-driven simulator, a real-I/O replay harness with cold-cache control,
  and an exact integer-only context-mixing codec. Experiment design, code and
  drafting were carried out with substantial assistance from Claude, an AI
  assistant from Anthropic; the author is responsible for the content.
keywords:
  - prefetching
  - lossless compression
  - context mixing
  - learned caching
  - data transfer
  - benchmarking
